@prefix dho:  <https://guoxiangng.github.io/dhamma-ontology/ns#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Coverage log: one record per text this project draws on (see DECISIONS.md D11).
# Hand-written. scripts/coverage.py combines it with the graph and the SuttaCentral
# canon list to produce COVERAGE.md. SHACL S10 fails the build if a text has no record.
#
# "modelledBy" is stated plainly: the project owner is not a teacher, and the modelling
# was drafted with an AI assistant. Nothing here has been reviewed by anyone qualified yet.

dho:t-sn46.51
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "All 24 statements of what fuels and starves the five hindrances and seven awakening factors, each as a nutriment node (object + kind of attention + effect). The opening statement (1.2) anchors both lists." ;
    dho:leftOut "Nothing doctrinal. The question (x.1) and conclusion (x.4) of each section restate the claim and are not cited separately." .

dho:t-sn46.53
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The timing advice: which awakening factors it is the right or wrong time to develop when the mind is sluggish (4.1, 7.1) or restless (10.1, 13.1), and 'mindfulness is always useful' (15.4)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting and the challenge from wanderers of other religions (1.1-3.1); the four fire similes (5, 8, 11, 14) that illustrate the advice; the repeated statements after each simile (6, 9, 12, 15.1-15.3); the reason given for each piece of advice, that a sluggish mind is hard or easy to stimulate and a restless one hard or easy to settle (4.3, 7.3, 10.3, 13.3): cited, but no field records it. Corrected 2026-11-15: the encoded note had claimed the reasons (D19)." .

dho:t-mn43
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Only the first absorption: its five factors (19.2-19.3), and that it gives up the five hindrances and possesses those five factors (20.2-20.4)." ;
    dho:leftOut "Most of the dialogue: wisdom and consciousness (2-6), feeling, perception and consciousness (7-9), what purified mind consciousness can know and how it is understood with the eye of wisdom (10-11), the goal of wisdom and conditions for right view (12-14), states of existence (15-17), what the first absorption is (18), the five faculties (21-22), vital forces and death vs cessation (23-25), and the releases of the heart (26-37)." .

dho:t-mn10
    dho:coverage dho:CitedOnly ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "One segment (36.2), recorded as a contested use of the word 'dhamma' and deliberately left without a sense." ;
    dho:leftOut "The whole teaching on the four kinds of mindfulness meditation. Its section on the five hindrances (knowing when each is present, how it arises, how it is given up) bears directly on this ontology and should come next." .

dho:t-mn148
    dho:coverage dho:CitedOnly ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Two segments (5.3, 6.8) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning an object of the mind." ;
    dho:leftOut "The six sets of six (sense fields, objects, consciousnesses, contacts, feelings, cravings) and the not-self argument built on them." .

dho:t-sn11.3
    dho:coverage dho:CitedOnly ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "One segment (10.2) as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning the Buddha's teaching." ;
    dho:leftOut "The banner simile and the recollection of the Buddha, the teaching and the Saṅgha as a remedy for fear." .

dho:t-dhp279
    dho:coverage dho:CitedOnly ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The first line of the verse ('All things are not-self') as evidence for 'dhamma' meaning any phenomenon." ;
    dho:leftOut "The rest of the verse, and the rest of the Path chapter (Dhp 273-289)." .

# A text we cite by reference only: we do not hold it, so its claims stay flagged as unverified.
dho:t-vism a dho:Text ;
    skos:prefLabel "Visuddhimagga IV.86"@en ;
    dho:layer dho:CommentaryLayer ;
    dho:coverage dho:ReferencedOnly ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from memory of the text, not checked against it" ;
    dho:encodes "Five pairings of a jhāna factor against a hindrance (citing the Peṭakopadesa)." ;
    dho:leftOut "Everything else. The text is not held; the pairings need checking against an edition before they can be marked verified." .

dho:t-mn44
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "One definition: 'Unification of the mind is immersion' (12.2). Found while checking an eval answer; it corrected decision D4, which had wrongly called this equation an interpretation." ;
    dho:leftOut "The rest of Dhammadinnā's answers: substantial reality, its origin, cessation and the practice leading there (2-5); grasping and the aggregates (6); substantialist view (7-8); the noble eightfold path and the three spectrums of practice (9-11); the bases, prerequisites and development of immersion (12.3-12.5); the three processes (13-15); the cessation of perception and feeling (16-21); the three feelings, their underlying tendencies and their counterparts (22-29), ending with 'extinguishment is the objective, destination, and culmination of the spiritual life' (29.15); and the Buddha's endorsement of her answers (30.4-30.5), which gives the definition its authority." .

dho:t-sn46.2
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Its 12 statements of what fuels the five hindrances and seven awakening factors (2-6, 9-15). They match SN 46.51 sections 1-12 (identical English; Pali differs only in punctuation and one spelling variant), so they were added as a second citation on the same claims, not as new claims." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile framing the teaching: as the body is sustained by food, so the hindrances and the awakening factors are sustained by fuel (1.2-1.3, 7, 8, 16). There is no pattern for similes yet." .

dho:t-sn46.22
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Its whole teaching: the list of the seven awakening factors (1.1, 1.3, 1.4), as citations on the existing list." .

dho:t-sn46.33
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The five corruptions of the mind as a list whose members are the same five qualities as the hindrances (2.1, 2.3, 2.4)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the five corruptions of native gold (1.1-1.8), and what the corruptions do: the mind is not pliable, workable or radiant, is brittle, and is not rightly immersed for the ending of defilements (2.1, 2.4). No pattern yet for similes or for what a quality does." .

dho:t-sn46.37
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Both lists (1.1, 1.3-1.7; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances weaken wisdom (1.1, 1.8); developing the awakening factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (2.1, 2.4)." ;
    dho:leftOut "That the hindrances are obstacles and corruptions of the heart, and the awakening factors are not (1.1, 1.8, 2.1, 2.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." .

dho:t-sn46.38
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Both lists (2.1, 2.2; 3.1, 3.2), and the teaching: when a noble disciple pays attention, applies the mind, concentrates wholeheartedly and actively listens to the teaching, the five hindrances are absent and the seven awakening factors are fully developed (1.1, 3.4)." .

dho:t-sn46.40
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Both lists (1.1, 1.3; 2.1, 2.3); the hindrances block wisdom and don't lead to extinguishment (1.1, 1.8); the awakening factors grow wisdom and lead to extinguishment (2.1, 2.4)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The Pali compounds 'making blind, sightless, ignorant' and 'on the side of distress' for the hindrances, and their opposites for the awakening factors (1.1, 2.1), which don't map cleanly onto a target concept; and the chapter's summary verse (3.0-3.4)." .

dho:t-sn46.1
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.4), and the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6, 1.12)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of dragons growing strong on the Himalayas and reaching the ocean (1.2-1.3), and the result 'acquiring great and abundant good qualities' (1.4, 1.13). No simile pattern yet." .

dho:t-sn46.5
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (1.5, 1.11); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.7)." ;
    dho:leftOut "As they are developed the mind is freed from the defilements of sensuality, desire to be reborn and ignorance, and knows it is freed (1.8-1.10). Needs the three defilements (āsava) as a list and a pattern for release." .

dho:t-sn46.7
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors slants, slopes and inclines to extinguishment (1.2, 2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of a bungalow's rafters inclining to the peak (1.1)." .

dho:t-sn46.11
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of creatures in the four postures depending on the earth (1.1-1.2)." .

dho:t-sn46.12
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the dawn as forerunner of the sunrise (1.1)." .

dho:t-sn46.13
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Rational application of mind is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one accomplished in it can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the dawn (1.1)." .

dho:t-sn46.17
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to going from the near shore to the far shore (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The verses (2.1-6.6): few cross to the far shore, the astute develop the bright, and those rightly developed in the awakening factors are quenched in this world." .

dho:t-sn46.19
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors brings one who practices them to the complete ending of suffering (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are 'noble and emancipating' (ariyā niyyānikā) (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." .

dho:t-sn46.20
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening (sambodhi) and extinguishment (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

dho:t-sn46.21
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Why they are called awakening factors: they lead to awakening (bodhi) (2.3, 2.6); the list (2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.5)." .

dho:t-sn46.24
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow, the awakening factors don't arise or cease (1.1-1.6). Rational application of mind: the hindrances don't arise or are given up, the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1-3.1). Corrected 2026-11-15: the results 'grow', 'given up' and 'fully developed' were described here but not in the claims (D19)." .

dho:t-sn46.31
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in diligence (1.1); a diligent mendicant can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "'Diligence is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." .

dho:t-sn46.32
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Skillful qualities are rooted in rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop the seven factors (1.2); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "'Rational application of mind is said to be the best of them' (1.1). Needs a pattern for ranking." .

dho:t-sn46.34
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to the realization of the fruit of knowledge and freedom (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." ;
    dho:leftOut "That the factors are not obstacles, hindrances or corruptions of the mind (1.1, 1.4). Needs a pattern for what a quality is or is not." .

dho:t-sn46.35
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Irrational application of mind: the hindrances arise and grow (1.1). Rational application of mind: the awakening factors arise and are fully developed (2.1). Corrected 2026-11-15: 'grow' and 'fully developed' are now in the claims (D19)." .

dho:t-sn46.36
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors leads to growth and progress (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.3)." .

dho:t-sn46.48
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Good friendship is the forerunner of the arising of the seven factors (1.2), and one with good friends can expect to develop them (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6). Same statements as SN 46.12, added as citations." ;
    dho:leftOut "The simile of the dawn (1.1)." .

dho:t-sn46.49
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Of interior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop and cultivate them (1.2), by the stock formula (1.3-1.6). Corrected 2026-11-15: 1.2-1.6 had been called abbreviated; they are untranslated in the English but given in the Pali (D19)." .

dho:t-sn46.50
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Of exterior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like good friendship (1.1); one with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate them (1.2), by the stock formula (1.3-1.6). Corrected 2026-11-15: 1.2-1.6 had been called abbreviated; they are untranslated in the English but given in the Pali (D19). The chapter's summary verse (2.0-2.4) is not a teaching." .

dho:t-sn46.25
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The list of the seven awakening factors (1.7)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The naming: the seven awakening factors are 'the seven principles that prevent decline' (aparihāniyā dhammā) (1.1, 1.3, 1.5, 1.8). Needs a pattern for what a quality is called." .

dho:t-sn46.26
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that leads to the ending of craving (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:leftOut "The chain: as they develop each factor, craving is given up; when craving is given up, deeds are given up; when deeds are given up, suffering is given up (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.9). Needs a pattern for chains of ending, which dependent origination will also need. Also the description of each factor as 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." .

dho:t-sn46.27
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that leads to the cessation of craving (1.1, 1.4, 2.3); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." .

dho:t-sn46.28
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that helps penetration (1.1, 1.5, 1.9, 2.9); the list (1.7); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:leftOut "With a mind that has developed each factor, they penetrate and shatter the mass of greed, hate and delusion for the first time (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.8); 'weakens' would understate 'shatter', so it waits for a better fit. Also 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." .

dho:t-sn46.29
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "Nothing else, developed like this, leads to giving up the things that tighten the fetters like the seven factors (1.1, 2.3); the list (1.3); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." ;
    dho:leftOut "What the things that tighten the fetters are: the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body and mind, where the fetters, shackles and attachments arise (3.1-3.8). Needs the six sense fields as a list and a pattern for 'X is where Y arises'." .

dho:t-sn46.41
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "All ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give up the three discriminations do so by developing the seven factors (1.2-1.4, 1.7-1.9); the list (1.6). The sutta doesn't name the three discriminations, so neither does the ontology." .

dho:t-sn46.43
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path for crushing Māra's army (1.1, 1.5, 1.8); the list (1.7)." .

dho:t-sn46.130
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The five higher fetters as a list (1.2, 1.4); the seven factors should be developed for their direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing and giving up (1.6, 1.12); and the formula variants: culminating in the removal of greed, hate and delusion (1.9), having freedom from death as their culmination (1.10), and inclining to extinguishment (1.11); and the seclusion formula at 1.8, which is in the Pali but not the English of that segment (added 2026-11-15, D19). The rest of the sutta is abbreviated in the source." .

dho:t-sn46.57
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:encodes "The perception of a skeleton is very fruitful and beneficial (1.2, 1.6), developed together with the awakening factors (1.4), with the stock formula (1.5); one of two results, enlightenment in this very life or non-return; great benefit, great sanctuary from the yoke, great inspiration and great ease." .

